CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
The atomic section around a store into a symbolic-size array (see
`symbolic_size_store_own_element`) is for values only. Counted as an atomic
access by the data-race encoding, it made both conflicting stores atomic and
the race between them disappeared (SUCCESSFUL), as it did for
pthread-race-challenges/per-thread-array-index-race and four other tasks.
Must stay FAILED.
